Author: Angel Robles-Fernandez [aut, cre], Jorge Soberon [aut]
Maintainer: Angel Robles-Fernandez <a.l.robles.fernandez@gmail.com>
Description:
  Estimation of environmental niches as bivariate normal ellipsoids from
  presence-only occurrence data, normalized against a user-supplied
  environmental background representing the accessible area M (Jimenez
  et al. 2019 <doi:10.1016/j.ecolmodel.2018.11.013>). Niche parameters
  (centroid mu, tolerances sigma, correlation rho) evolve along a
  phylogeny under Brownian motion or Ornstein-Uhlenbeck processes, or an
  independent-species null model. Inference proceeds by fast multistart
  MAP optimization (C++ backend via ucminfcpp, warm starts via xnicher)
  with boundary diagnostics, or by full Bayesian inference through
  bundled Stan models when cmdstanr/CmdStan are installed. All Stan
  models support reduce_sum parallelisation for HPC workflows.
